@startuml dyn-deployment-process
!include include/palette.puml

title Dynamic: deployment process of app #1 workorders in tdd, uat and prod (§7.0, §7.2, ADR-IR33, ADR-IR34)

<style>
activityDiagram {
  activity {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_OCTOPUS
    MaximumWidth 300
  }
  diamond {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_OCTOPUS
  }
  arrow {
    LineColor #555555
  }
  note {
    MaximumWidth 560
  }
  .wake {
    BackgroundColor $C_WAKE
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_WAKE
  }
  .manual {
    BackgroundColor $C_OCTOPUS
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_OCTOPUS
  }
  .pin {
    BackgroundColor $C_ARGO
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_ARGO
  }
  .azure {
    BackgroundColor $C_AZURE
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_AZURE
  }
  .nonprod {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_NONPROD_TIER
    FontColor $C_NONPROD_TIER
    LineThickness 2
  }
  .prod {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_PROD_TIER
    FontColor $C_PROD_TIER
    LineThickness 2
  }
  .incluster {
    BackgroundColor $C_K8S
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_K8S
  }
}
</style>

start
:A release of workorders deploys to one environment.
Channel Default: releases from the Codefresh
pipeline workorders/release, lifecycle
platform-standard: tdd automatically, then
uat and prod by hand.
Channel Hotfix: releases by Release Managers,
lifecycle platform-hotfix: uat, then prod;
:0 Wake environment
Deploy a Release of platform-wake to the same
environment, deployment condition Always,
waits for the child deployment; <<wake>>
note right
  Every environment and channel, no key in workorders:
  platform-wake runs env-wake in infra-nonprod (tdd, uat)
  or infra-prod (prod) and fails when the wake fails
end note
switch (Environment?)
case ()
  :**tdd** on aks-platform-nonprod:
  automatic, channel Default only; <<nonprod>>
  fork
    :5 Update Argo CD image tags
    pin, then wait for Healthy; <<pin>>
  fork again
    :6 Read deployment secrets
    Azure CLI as azure-workorders-tdd on k8s-tdd:
    db-app-password and ai-openai-apikey of
    kv-workorders-t-<hash4>, outputs for step 9; <<azure>>
  end fork
  fork
    :7 Verify version;
  fork again
    :8 Smoke test
    Degraded fails;
  end fork
  :9 Acceptance tests (TDD only)
  k8s-tdd, container platform/ci-dotnet,
  package ChurchBulletin.AcceptanceTests,
  5 NUnit workers, 30 minutes,
  TRX files as artifacts; <<incluster>>
  :12 Report platform/tdd status
  condition Always; skipped while
  GitHub.StatusEnabled is False;
case ()
  :**uat** on aks-platform-nonprod:
  by hand, channels Default and Hotfix; <<nonprod>>
  if (Channel Hotfix?) then (yes)
    :1 Hotfix justification
    Release Managers; <<manual>>
  else (no)
  endif
  :5 Update Argo CD image tags
  pin, then wait for Healthy; <<pin>>
  fork
    :7 Verify version;
  fork again
    :8 Smoke test
    Degraded accepted;
  end fork
  :10 UAT sign-off
  UAT Approvers; <<manual>>
  :11 UAT sign-off guard
  platform-sod-guard: the automation
  user answers only with a run reason;
case ()
  :**prod** on aks-platform-prod: by hand,
  channels Default and Hotfix; blocked on
  weekends by prod-weekend-freeze-workorders
  unless overridden with a reason; <<prod>>
  if (Channel Hotfix?) then (yes)
    :1 Hotfix justification
    Release Managers; <<manual>>
  else (no)
  endif
  :2 Prod go/no-go
  Prod Approvers; <<manual>>
  :3 Separation-of-duties guard
  platform-sod-guard: creator rule
  of Platform.SoDMode, run reason
  of the automation user;
  :4 Back up database
  platform-db-backup on k8s-prod: Job
  from CronJob db-backup-workorders-prod,
  waits up to 1800 s; <<incluster>>
  :5 Update Argo CD image tags
  pin, then wait for Healthy; <<pin>>
  fork
    :7 Verify version;
  fork again
    :8 Smoke test
    Degraded accepted;
  end fork
endswitch
:Deployment ends: success, or failed at the first failing step;
note right
  Steps run in the order of deployment_process.ocl (numbers 0 to 12);
  a step outside its environment scope is skipped. 6 and 8 start with the
  previous step (start trigger StartWithPrevious), so 5 and 6, and 7 and 8,
  run in parallel; the next step waits for both. Run condition:
  every earlier step succeeded, except 1 (variable condition, read through
  Octopus.Step.ConditionVariableExpression: no error and channel Hotfix)
  and 12 (Always: reports failure too).
  5: Octopus.ArgoCDUpdateImageTags on hosted-ubuntu. Direct commit of newTag
  for apps/workorders/ui-server, worker and db-migrator (feed acr-apps, not
  acquired) to gitops/apps/workorders/envs/<env>/app/kustomization.yaml.
  Sync off: argocd-nonprod or argocd-prod polls main, runs the PreSync Job
  db-migrate, then rolls out. The step waits until the Application annotated
  workorders and <env> (workorders-app-<env>) is Healthy, up to
  Argo.VerificationTimeoutSeconds (900); one automatic retry.
  7: App.BaseUrl + /_version starts with the package version. 8: /_healthcheck
  Healthy within 150 s. 3, 5, 7, 8, 11, 12 run on hosted-ubuntu.
end note
stop

legend right
  |<$C_WAKE>    | Wake (Deploy a Release of platform-wake) |
  |<$C_OCTOPUS>    | Manual intervention (team) |
  |<$C_ARGO>    | Pin commit; Argo CD applies |
  |<$C_AZURE>    | Azure CLI with the app's OIDC account |
  |<$C_K8S>    | In-cluster step on worker pool k8s-<env> |
  |<#FFFFFF>    | Script on hosted-ubuntu |
endlegend
@enduml
